---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

---
<BaseLayout title="How to Get Off the Barracuda Blocklist (BBRB)" description="Barracuda blocklist removal: why listings happen, the removal request process, and realistic timelines."  
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["Email Authentication", "/email-authentication/"], ["Email Deliverability", "/email-deliverability/"], ["Barracuda Removal"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-deliverability/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Deliverability</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Barracuda Removal</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Get Off the Barracuda Blocklist</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      Barracuda's BBRB (b.barracudacentral.org) is reputation-based: listings follow observed spam
      behavior or poor sending practices from your IP, and removal follows demonstrated good
      behavior plus a request.
    </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Barracuda triggers</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Trigger</th><th>Prevention</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">Spam-trap hits</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Never mail purchased lists</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">Complaints</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">One-click unsubscribe</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">New IP volume</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Warm over weeks</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
<nav class="pd-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#why-ips-land-on-it">Why IPs land on it</a></li>
        <li><a href="#the-removal-process">The removal process</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-not-to-do">What not to do</a></li>
        <li><a href="#related">Related</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 id="why-ips-land-on-it">Why IPs land on it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Spamtrap hits, usually from stale or scraped lists.</li>
        <li>High complaint rates from Barracuda's customer base.</li>
        <li>New IPs with sudden volume and no reputation history.</li>
        <li>Missing authentication or reverse DNS, which weigh into the score.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="the-removal-process">The removal process</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li><strong>Verify the listing</strong> with the <a href="/blacklist-checker/">blacklist checker</a> (noting that some lists refuse public-resolver queries, in which case check on Barracuda's own lookup page).</li>
        <li><strong>Fix sending practices first</strong>: authentication (<a href="/spf-record-checker/">SPF</a>, <a href="/dkim-record-checker/">DKIM</a>, <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/">DMARC</a>), PTR, list hygiene, volume ramp.</li>
        <li><strong>Submit the removal request</strong> at Barracuda Central's lookup/removal form. One request per IP; include what you fixed.</li>
        <li><strong>Wait the stated interval.</strong> First requests typically process within 24-72 hours; repeated or unfixed listings take longer and repeat-listing shortens patience.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="what-not-to-do">What not to do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Resubmitting daily: it does not accelerate and looks like automation abuse.</li>
        <li>Requesting removal while the spam source is still active; relisting is faster the second time.</li>
        <li>Switching to a fresh IP instead of fixing practices: the new IP inherits the behavior, and old listings linger.</li>
      </ul>
      
<h2 id="related">Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/remove-from-spamhaus-blocklist/">Spamhaus removal</a> and <a href="/sorbs-delisting-guide/">SORBS delisting</a></li>
        <li><a href="/why-emails-go-to-spam/">Why emails go to spam</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does Barracuda delisting take?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Usually within an hour of an approved request, and the block decays naturally in days if the sending behavior stops.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Why did my IP get listed?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Barracuda reacts to spam-trap hits, complaint rates, and sudden volume from new IPs. A new server sending cold email is the classic trigger.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I prevent future listings?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Authenticate with SPF, DKIM, and enforced DMARC, warm new IPs slowly, and keep complaint rates low. Listings follow behavior, not luck.</p></details></div>
      </div>
</BaseLayout>
